From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: show a window's exposed parts at once in an external shell session

Purpose: keep windows under a dragged window drawn in the X11 sessions.
Windows behavior: windows that a moving window uncovers are redrawn while
it moves (with "Show window contents while dragging").
Wine before: on an Expose event from the host, a window with a surface
only added the exposed rectangle to the surface's bounds. A thread waiting
for messages flushes its surfaces before it waits, but the Expose events
it handles inside that wait post no message, so it went back to waiting
without flushing: the parts of an idle window (Notepad behind a folder
window dragged by bridge-wm) stayed black until the window got a message,
such as the pointer moving over it.
Change: with the opt-in, flush the surface as soon as a part is exposed,
as Wine already does for surfaces with an alpha mask.
Evidence: drag a folder window over Notepad in the nested X11 session
(Luna and classic): the uncovered part of Notepad was black during and
after the drag, and is drawn with the change.
Scope: only with WIN4WINE_EXTERNAL_SHELL.
---
 dlls/win32u/window.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/window.c b/dlls/win32u/window.c
index 44ed14d..6c2c0cb 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/window.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/window.c
@@ -2390,7 +2390,9 @@ static BOOL expose_window_surface( HWND hwnd, UINT flags, const RECT *rect, UINT
         add_bounds_rect( &surface->bounds, &exposed_rect );
     }
     window_surface_unlock( surface );
-    if (surface->alpha_mask) window_surface_flush( surface );
+    /* win4wine: the host exposed this part of a window that another one
+     * covered; show it now, as an idle thread flushes only on its next message */
+    if (surface->alpha_mask || win4wine_external_shell()) window_surface_flush( surface );
     window_surface_release( surface );
     return TRUE;
 }
